solution.p:
We start with the equation s(1-m)=w and substitute in what we know. The value for m should be 0.35 and the value for w should be 16\text{.} So we have the equation
\begin{aligned}
s(1-0.35) \amp= 16\\
s(0.65) \amp= 16
\end{aligned}
Now to solve for s\text{,} divide on each side by 0.65\text{:}
\begin{aligned}
\divideunder{s(0.65)}{0.65} \amp= \divideunder{16}{0.65}\\
s \amp= {24.62}
\end{aligned}
So the shelf price is $24.62.
